MinIO on openRuyi
================

Set MINIO_ROOT_USER and MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD in /etc/sysconfig/minio before
starting the service. The file is readable only by root; systemd passes its
settings to the service running as the minio user. Configuration is preserved
on package upgrades.

Start the service with:

    systemctl enable --now minio.service

The default S3 API listens on port 9000 and the Console on port 9001. Data is
stored in /var/lib/minio/data. To use other disks or endpoints, adjust
MINIO_VOLUMES and MINIO_OPTS and ensure the minio user can access the data.
Data is retained when the package is removed.

Use journalctl -u minio.service to inspect service logs.
